  "text": "**Step 1: Falsification**\n\n- **Solution 1 (12):** The number matches my recollection of Doyle's results on quadratic maps over Q with nonabelian automorphism group, but I can't verify that from memory. The argument has gaps. It asserts that the 6 period-3 points form one size-6 orbit without ruling out other configurations. It also asserts that an explicit map attains 12 without giving one, and its orbit bookkeeping (which orbits can be rational, and how strictly preperiodic points can land on the fixed-point orbit) is not checked.\n- **Solution 2 (4):** Falls apart early. It asserts that a degree-2 map's automorphism group must be dihedral and that only n = 3 is possible, with no argument. The claim that the rational preperiodic points are bounded by the rational torsion on the unit circle is unsupported. Its own example, 1/z², does not show the maximum is 4.\n- **Solution 3 (10):** Relies on a claimed Yap classification that includes A₄ as an automorphism group. A₄ does not occur as the automorphism group of a degree-2 rational map, so the premise is wrong. The cited result also appears misremembered.\n\nNo solution survives falsification with the certainty the protocol requires. Solution 1 is the most plausible, but its derivation is incomplete, so I can't select it at confidence 4 or higher.\n\nCHOICE: NONE\nCONFIDENCE: 3",
